# VFZ Work Schedule integrations - crontab
#
# Install for the service user:
#     crontab -e          # paste the lines below
#     crontab -l          # confirm
#
# Or drop in as a system crontab, adding a user column between the schedule
# and the command:
#     sudo cp vfz-workschedule-emails.crontab /etc/cron.d/vfz-workschedule
#     sudo chmod 644 /etc/cron.d/vfz-workschedule

# Cron runs in the system timezone, usually UTC. Both jobs decide "today" and
# the notification window from [emails]/[db_resync] timezone in segredo.ini,
# but the schedules below are clock time -- so pin cron to the same zone or the
# two drift apart at every DST change.
CRON_TZ=Africa/Johannesburg

# Cron sets almost no PATH. flock and date must be resolvable.
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

# Both entries call a wrapper, never an interpreter path directly. The wrapper
# locates the venv -- which does not have to be called .venv -- and checks it
# can import the dependencies before running. A crontab line naming
# .venv/bin/python on a box whose venv is named something else exits 127 before
# Python starts, and with the output discarded that is completely silent.
# Set VFZ_PYTHON here to override the search on an unusual box.

# Silence cron's own mail; the wrapper writes its own log and everything goes
# to SolarWinds regardless.
MAILTO=""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DB Resync - daily at 03:00
#
# The wrapper resolves the shared venv at the repo root, takes a lock and
# writes its own log, so none of that has to live in this line.
#
# Replaces the whole table with whoever is off today. Runs every day, not just
# weekdays: a weekend run writes zero rows (weekends are never non-working
# days) and Monday's 03:00 run repopulates before the first Emails run at
# 08:00. Five hours of margin, so a slow or failed run has room to be noticed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
0 3 * * * /srv/vfz_work_schedule/vfz_workschedule_db_resync/scripts/run-resync.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Emails - every 10 minutes, 08:00 to 17:50, Monday to Friday
#
# 8-17 with */10 gives 08:00 through 17:50. notify_end_hour is EXCLUSIVE, so
# 17:50 is the last slot inside the window and nothing is wasted.
#
# The window is deliberately expressed twice: here, and as notify_start_hour /
# notify_end_hour in segredo.ini. Cron decides when the process starts; the
# in-code check is the backstop that stops a mistimed or manual run commenting
# at 03:00. KEEP THE TWO IN AGREEMENT - they are currently 08:00-18:00.
#
# The wrapper takes a lock, so a run that overruns its ten minutes is not
# joined by the next one. That matters: two concurrent runs could both read an
# empty notification history and post the same comment twice.
#
# No separate upstream-late entry is needed. Running every ten minutes means
# the 08:10 slot already falls just past upstream_grace_minutes, so a missed
# resync is reported within ten minutes rather than an hour.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*/10 8-17 * * 1-5 /srv/vfz_work_schedule/vfz_workschedule_emails/scripts/run-notifier.sh
